# forge crontab — installed by ../deploy.sh, edit it here not with crontab -e.
#
# Alert in Slack when bastion Vaultwarden falls behind. Runs the deployed copy,
# not a git clone, so a branch switch cannot make it vanish.
@reboot /home/robby/homelab-deployed/forge/scripts/vaultwarden-version-check.sh

# Keep ollama on the GPU. GDM unloads the nvidia kernel modules a few minutes after
# every boot, which leaves the container unable to reach the driver; inference then
# silently moves to the CPU and the agent appears to stop responding. See the header
# of gpu-guard.sh, including the root fix.
*/15 5-22 * * * /home/robby/homelab-deployed/forge/scripts/gpu-guard.sh

# Report forge's own health to #homelab-logs, between bastion's report at 7:00 and
# the digest at 7:30, so the digest covers a report from the same morning.
10 7 * * * /home/robby/homelab-deployed/forge/scripts/health-report.py

# Read the hosts' reports from #homelab-logs and decide what deserves a human.
#
# Hourly triage posts only when something escalates, so a quiet day is silent.
# Bounded to forge's waking hours -- reports posted while forge is off are picked up
# by the cursor on the next run, because Slack Socket Mode has no replay.
0 6-22 * * * /home/robby/homelab-deployed/forge/scripts/health-digest.py --triage

# The daily digest runs after bastion reports at 7:00 and always posts, so silence is
# itself the signal bastion's watchdog looks for.
30 7 * * * /home/robby/homelab-deployed/forge/scripts/health-digest.py --digest
